    <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">KnownHost is a compelling choice for developers and self-hosters who want NVMe storage without paying premium prices. The $5/mo entry plan with 25GB NVMe, 2TB bandwidth, and 2 dedicated IPs is genuinely rare — most providers at this price point use SATA SSDs or limit you to 1 IP. The 20-year track record since 2006 adds confidence that KnownHost will be around for the long haul. The three datacenter locations (Atlanta, Seattle, Amsterdam) cover North America and Europe well, though the absence of APAC is a gap for global projects. If NVMe storage at entry-level pricing matters to you, KnownHost is one of the best picks in this segment. For the absolute lowest price or global datacenter coverage, RackNerd ($1.99/mo, 8 locations) or Vultr ($2.50/mo, 32 locations) remain strong alternatives.</p>
